WEBVTT

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:47.110
Gentlemen, this is a corpse.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.220
There is a tradition among medical students that dealing with death humorously makes things easier.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:01.690
It doesn't.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.140
There may be a successful joke about death in the abstract,

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.060
but I have never heard it.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.300
About death in the particular?

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.050
Believe me, there is nothing funny at all.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.050
I have been a pathologist for over 25 years.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.790
I haven't been able to get a single laugh out of it yet.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.850
For some of you, this will be unpleasant.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.400
For a few, perhaps, perhaps impossible.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.970
Fixed firmly in your heads that seven hours...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.560
This was a living soul housed in an edifice constructed by a supremely capable architect.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.290
We're about to violate it.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.990
And when you do, you will help yourselves immeasurably as physicians and healers

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:54.190
if you do so tenderly and with love.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.580
Our purpose here today is to determine the cause of death.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.580
We will follow the method of Rokotansky, which is to remove the visceral organs intact.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.990
First, we will make a cruciate incision from the suprasternal notch to the pubis.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.580
And then, transversely as well. Thus.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.990
Seven hours ago, this was a living soul.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.510
Well, that settles, and I'm not leaving my body to science.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.950
You kidding? I may not even die.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.640
That Aaron's puts on a great show, though, doesn't he?

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.200
Yeah, he doesn't get any laughs, though.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.140
All right, so I'm nervous.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.660
You eating with us, Marsh?

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.680
No, I can't. I have to work the lab tonight.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.090
We got nurses. We can get one for you.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.220
Pretty? Who cares? They're alive, aren't they?

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:59.100
I'm saving myself till the right girl comes along.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.300
